{"question": "The US and Iran are talking at the UN. So why is oil still going up?", "country": "IR", "voice_speed": 1.02, "gap": 0.2, "cover": ["PEACE TALKS: ON.", "OIL: $105.", "WHY?"], "region": "OIL / STRAIT OF HORMUZ", "places": {"HORMUZ": {"id": "HORMUZ", "name": "Strait of Hormuz", "lat": 26.56, "lon": 56.25}}, "lines": [{"text": "Peace talks at the UN. And oil just jumped past 105 dollars.", "src": [0], "context": false, "note": "The National, 24 Sep 2026", "scene": {"type": "barrel", "value": "$105", "n": 105.33, "max": 125, "label": "Brent crude, per barrel", "detail": "+2.2% today, +5.5% this week", "ref": {"n": 70, "label": "PRE-WAR ~$70"}}}, {"text": "The reason is here. Before the war, over 100 ships a day sailed through Hormuz.", "src": [1], "context": false, "note": "DTN, 22 Sep 2026", "scene": {"type": "tankers", "mode": "before", "place": "HORMUZ", "lane": [[54.9, 26.15], [55.6, 26.35], [56.2, 26.55], [56.6, 26.42], [56.85, 25.9], [57.4, 25.45], [58.2, 25.2]], "head": "{n}+ ships a day", "n_from": 0, "n": 100, "notes": ["before the war", "20M barrels a day"]}}, {"text": "On Monday, just 2 cargo ships made it through.", "src": [1], "context": false, "note": "DTN, 22 Sep 2026", "scene": {"type": "tankers", "mode": "after", "place": "HORMUZ", "lane": [[54.9, 26.15], [55.6, 26.35], [56.2, 26.55], [56.6, 26.42], [56.85, 25.9], [57.4, 25.45], [58.2, 25.2]], "head": "{n} ships", "n_from": 100, "n": 2, "notes": ["Monday, 21 Sep", "down more than 90%"]}}, {"text": "In New York, Iran offered a 60 day ceasefire and a phased reopening.", "src": [2], "context": false, "note": "The National, 23 Sep 2026", "scene": {"type": "statement", "lines": ["60-day ceasefire.", "Phased reopening.", "Lift the blockade."], "flag": "IR"}}, {"text": "Trump's answer: the blockade stays until Iran shows goodwill first.", "src": [2], "context": false, "note": "The National, 23 Sep 2026", "scene": {"type": "statement", "lines": ["Blockade stays.", "Goodwill first."], "flag": "US"}}, {"text": "So traders keep paying for the risk. Brent is up around 50 percent on pre-war prices.", "src": [3, 0], "context": false, "note": "Wikipedia / The National", "scene": {"type": "chart", "head": "$70 → $105", "label": "Brent crude, per barrel", "min": 50, "max": 130, "grid": [70, 100], "points": [["PRE-WAR", 70], ["31 MAR", 118.35], ["1 JUL", 71.57], ["22 SEP", 99.25], ["24 SEP", 105.33]]}}, {"text": "Analysts say a real deal to reopen the strait could pull Brent back to the low 90s.", "src": [4], "context": false, "note": "Capital.com, via The National", "scene": {"type": "statement", "lines": ["Reopen the strait.", "Brent: low $90s?"]}}], "sources": [{"n": 0, "outlet": "The National", "title": "Oil prices top $105 as hopes fade for US-Iran breakthrough", "url": "https://www.thenationalnews.com/business/energy/2026/09/24/oil-prices-top-105-as-hopes-fade-for-us-iran-breakthrough/"}, {"n": 1, "outlet": "DTN", "title": "Oil Below $100 Bbl as U.S.-Iran Diplomacy Awaited at U.N.", "url": "https://www.dtnpf.com/agriculture/web/ag/news/world-policy/article/2026/09/22/oil-100-bbl-u-s-iran-diplomacy-u-n-2"}, {"n": 2, "outlet": "The National", "title": "Iran presents US with road map for regionwide ceasefire and Hormuz reopening", "url": "https://www.thenationalnews.com/news/mena/2026/09/23/iran-us-meeting-new-york/"}, {"n": 3, "outlet": "Wikipedia", "title": "2026 Iran war fuel crisis", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Iran_war_fuel_crisis"}, {"n": 4, "outlet": "The National", "title": "Oil at $100 a barrel as focus remains on Iran peace talks and Saudi supply recovery", "url": "https://www.thenationalnews.com/business/energy/2026/09/23/oil-at-100-a-barrel-as-focus-remains-on-iran-peace-talks-and-saudi-supply-recovery/"}], "caption": "The US and Iran are talking at the UN, but Brent just topped $105. Before the war 100+ ships a day passed through Hormuz. On Monday, 2 did. Until the strait reopens, the risk stays in the price.", "hashtags": ["oil", "iran", "hormuz", "trump", "outpost"]}
